AB  - Some sampling plots were selected in 2 forest farms of Southern Anhui Province and surveyed in December, 1999 and January, 2000. The result showed that the ratio of beneficial to harmful organism species number in Pinus massoniana stands was 1.26, and the ratio of beneficial to pest individual number was 0.62 among the 62 kinds of insects and spiders being found out, belonging to 35 families of 12 orders. The species number of natural enemy was slightly larger than that of pest. The dominant groups were Diptera, Homoptera, Coleoptera, Lepidoptera, Hymenoptera and Araneae. The species number of phytophagous, predatory, parasitic and spider groups was 30, 8, 10 and 20 respectively. The total species and individual number fluctuated a little during the two months because some organisms were acting. The ratio of beneficial to harmful organism and index of diversity of Daigongshan where Beauveria bassiana was applied against pests were larger than those of Magushan where pesticide was overused. The arthropods hid under the barks and in the branches and leaves in winter.
